{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The fund’s contractual partner—the adviser or other unitary-fee provider—bears the economic shortfall: it must cover fund expenses exceeding the agreed fee revenue. The fund’s service providers are still owed by the fund under their contracts; if the sponsor fails to pay, the fund remains liable (and ultimately shareholders bear the cost)."}}
